# Italian Sausage Soup with White Beans and Spinach

**Recipe ID:** R003  
**Source:** Kellie  
**Course:** Dinner, Lunch, Soup  
**Cuisine:** Italian  
**Prep Time:** 5 minutes  
**Cook Time:** 15 minutes  
**Total Time:** 20 minutes  
**Yield:** 8 servings

A hearty Italian sausage soup made with cannellini beans, spinach, tomatoes, and ditalini pasta. Ready in about 30 minutes using simple pantry ingredients.

## Ingredients

- 1 pound mild Italian sausage, casing removed
- 1 large Vidalia onion, diced
- 2 garlic cloves, minced
- 1 tablespoon Italian seasoning
- 5 cups chicken stock
- 1 (14.5-ounce) can diced tomatoes
- 1 (15.5-ounce) can cannellini beans, rinsed and drained
- 1/2 cup small pasta (ditalini recommended)
- 2 cups baby spinach
- Grated Parmesan cheese, for serving

## Instructions

1. Heat a large pot or Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add the sausage, breaking it into small pieces as it browns. Cook until no longer pink. Transfer the sausage to a bowl with a slotted spoon, leaving about 1 tablespoon of the rendered fat in the pot.
2. Add the diced onion to the pot and cook until translucent, about 4–5 minutes. Stir in the garlic and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.
3. Stir in the Italian seasoning and about **1/4 cup** of the chicken stock, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom of the pot.
4. Add the diced tomatoes, cannellini beans, cooked sausage, and remaining chicken stock. Stir in the ditalini pasta and bring to a boil. Cook for **6–7 minutes**, or until the pasta is al dente.
5. Stir in the spinach until wilted. Serve immediately, topped with grated Parmesan cheese.

## Serving Information

- Makes 8 servings.

## Refrigerator Storage

Allow the soup to cool before transferring it to airtight containers. Refrigerate leftovers for up to 4 days.

## Freezer Storage

Freeze without the Parmesan garnish in airtight freezer-safe containers. For best texture, freeze before adding the pasta or cook the pasta separately and add it when reheating.

## Reheating

- **Microwave:** Heat in 30-second intervals, stirring between each, until hot.
- **Stovetop:** Reheat over medium-low heat, adding a splash of chicken stock if needed to thin the soup.

## Notes

- Mild or hot Italian sausage may be used.
- Ditalini is recommended, but other small pasta shapes work well.
- Garnish each serving with freshly grated Parmesan cheese.
- Spinach should be stirred in at the very end to keep it bright and tender.
